{ ==========================================================================
  IND_S16S_ELEVEN  --  the last eleven chart patterns, as a subchart ribbon

  Build_ID 260913.  DETECTION ONLY.  Places no orders, holds no position.

  P33 upthrust / P35 break of structure / P37 change of character
  / P13 bear flag / P14 bear pennant / P41 WR4 / P42 WR7
  / P43 key reversal / P45 prior session low break / P47 horn top
  / P48 pipe top

  WHY A RIBBON AND NOT LABELS ON PRICE

    The eleven together mark 197,095 bars.  That is denser than the six
    convergence patterns (148,748) which already forced the ribbon on
    2026-08-31.  P41 alone is 82,258 -- one bar in five.  Text labels lose
    to that density in WIDTH, not in height, so lanes cannot rescue them;
    the ruling of 2026-08-31 (present everything, keep it clean) lands here
    as a second ribbon.

  TWO SKELETONS, AND THE ROWS SAY SO

    The scan that defined these calls the split out explicitly, so the
    ribbon groups by it rather than by density alone.  Rows 1-8 read OHLC
    directly.  Rows 9-11 read pivot LEVELS, and are the only three that
    carry structure rather than shape.

      row 11  P37  change of character   12,675
      row 10  P33  upthrust              18,003
      row  9  P35  break of structure    24,132     <- pivot skeleton
      row  8  P45  prior session low      1,463
      row  7  P48  pipe top               4,973
      row  6  P47  horn top               5,020
      row  5  P14  bear pennant           5,883
      row  4  P43  key reversal           8,308
      row  3  P13  bear flag             12,041
      row  2  P42  WR7                   44,455
      row  1  P41  WR4                   82,258     <- bar skeleton

    Within each group the densest row sits at the bottom, the same
    ordering IND_S16S_CONV6 and the label lanes in IND_S16S_P29 use.

  THE ONE-BAR LAG, AND WHY IT IS CORRECT RATHER THAN TOLERATED

    The scan skips any bar whose NEXT bar opens a new session, because the
    fractal test needs that next bar.  So the classification of a bar is
    not decidable on that bar -- not by this code, and not by a trader
    either.  This file therefore classifies bar [1] and marks the result on
    bar [0].

    A mark means "confirmed here", not "the shape ended here".  It is the
    same convention the pivot chain in IND_S16S_P29 has always used, and it
    is what a live chart can actually honour.

  DEVICES, ALL ZERO-PARAMETER

    rank            widest of the last N.  N = 4 and N = 7 are Crabel's,
                    accepted by ruling on 2026-08-31 and recorded as
                    BORROWED, not derived.
    shadow vs body  "long upper shadow" written as a comparison -- upper
                    shadow greater than the body.  Nothing to tune.
    gap vs shadow   "two highs at a similar level" takes its tolerance from
                    the bars themselves: the difference between the highs
                    smaller than the shorter of the two upper shadows.
    resolution      the bear flag carries no bar count.  The drift runs
                    until one side gives -- close under the pole low, or
                    the pole high exceeded -- so "how long is a flag" is
                    never asked.

  THE FLAG POLE LIST

    Several poles can be live at once.  Measured on the full series the
    list never exceeds THREE, so four slots is one spare; the fifth would
    increment v_Ovf, which the tally prints.  A silent cap is how a
    population quietly stops being a population.

    A pole is NOT killed by a session break.  The scan carries a branch
    that says it is, and that branch is unreachable behind the session
    guard -- measured: reached 0 times, while 419 flags (3.48% of P13)
    genuinely span a break.  This file reproduces the CODE, which is what
    the reference numbers came from, and says so here rather than quietly
    matching a comment instead.

  COUNTERS ARE NOT GATED BY Enable_

    Lesson of 2026-08-31: in build 260850 an Enable_ input gated v_Ok, so
    switching a pattern off stopped it being REGISTERED, not just drawn.
    "I do not want to see it" silently became "it was never measured".
    Here every counter runs unconditionally and Enable_ touches colour only.

  ACCEPTANCE, printed on the last bar as ELEVEN TALLY

    bars 421,506   pole_overflow 0
    P33 18003  P35 24132  P37 12675  P13 12041  P14  5883  P41 82258
    P42 44455  P43  8308  P45  1463  P47  5020  P48  4973

    NOT VERIFIED IN MC12 YET.  Those come from
    scripts/research/s16s_eleven_pla_model.py, which replays these
    predicates through THIS file's window -- seven bars of warm-up, empty
    state machines at bar 1, the one-bar lag -- and then diffs bar by bar
    against s16s_eleven_scan.py.  Zero disagreements across all eleven.

    bars= is 421,513 minus this file's own warm-up, and the warm-up is 7
    because High[7] is the deepest reference made here.  Read bars= as
    "after this file's warm-up", NEVER as "the chart's length" -- on
    2026-08-31 that confusion was written into three documents.

  ONE CSV IS NOT THE OTHER CSV

    2026-09-01: the desktop and the laptop each ran the defining scan on a
    CSV of 421,513 rows spanning the same first and last bar, and disagreed
    on ten of the eleven -- P41 82,209 vs 82,258, P45 1,477 vs 1,463.  The
    CSV is gitignored, so nothing in the repo could catch it.

    The numbers above are the LAPTOP's, md5 47e4054ff31b086df392bb3022e90e03.
    The scan now stamps that md5 into its json.  On the desktop, expect the
    desktop's own figures and compare against those, exactly as
    S16S_DESKTOP_BASELINE_20260901.md already rules for IND_S16S_P29.

  HOW TO SET IT UP
    Apply to a SUBCHART, not the price pane, and not the CONV6 pane.
    Style tab: every plot to Point, or a thick line.
    Scaling tab: fixed range 0 .. 12 so the eleven rows sit evenly.
  ======================================================================== }

inputs:
    Build_ID                ( 260913 ),
    Sess_Day_Start          ( 845   ),
    Sess_Day_End            ( 1345  ),
    Sess_Night_Start        ( 1500  ),
    Sess_Night_End          ( 500   ),
    Enable_P41              ( 1     ),     { WR4,               82,258 }
    Enable_P42              ( 1     ),     { WR7,               44,455 }
    Enable_P13              ( 1     ),     { bear flag,         12,041 }
    Enable_P43              ( 1     ),     { key reversal,       8,308 }
    Enable_P14              ( 1     ),     { bear pennant,       5,883 }
    Enable_P47              ( 1     ),     { horn top,           5,020 }
    Enable_P48              ( 1     ),     { pipe top,           4,973 }
    Enable_P45              ( 1     ),     { prior session low,  1,463 }
    Enable_P35              ( 1     ),     { break of structure,24,132 }
    Enable_P33              ( 1     ),     { upthrust,          18,003 }
    Enable_P37              ( 1     ),     { change of char,    12,675 }
    Col_Bar                 ( DarkGray  ),  { rows 1-8,  bar skeleton }
    Col_Flag                ( DarkRed   ),  { P13 / P14, the drift pair }
    Col_Pivot               ( Blue      ),  { rows 9-11, pivot skeleton }
    Col_Choch               ( Magenta   ),  { P37, the rarest structure }
    Col_Idle                ( Black     ),  { leave near the background }
    Print_Events            ( 0     );

arrays:
    v_PoH[4]                ( 0 ),          { pole high }
    v_PoL[4]                ( 0 ),          { pole low }
    v_PoN[4]                ( 0 ),          { drift bars survived }
    v_PoCv[4]               ( 0 ),          { 1 while ranges keep shrinking }
    v_PoLast[4]             ( 0 );          { previous drift bar range }

variables:
    v_In_Day                ( False ),
    v_In_Night              ( False ),
    v_In_Sess               ( False ),
    v_Sess_First            ( False ),
    v_BIS                   ( 0     ),     { bars into the session }
    v_Go                    ( False ),     { the scan guard, one bar lagged }
    v_Rng                   ( 0     ),
    v_CurLo                 ( 0     ),
    v_CurSet                ( False ),
    v_SessLo                ( 0     ),
    v_SessSet               ( False ),
    v_HiPv                  ( 0     ),
    v_HiSet                 ( False ),
    v_ArmHi                 ( False ),
    v_LoPv                  ( 0     ),
    v_LoSet                 ( False ),
    v_ArmLo                 ( False ),
    v_UpLast                ( False ),
    v_NPole                 ( 0     ),
    v_Ovf                   ( 0     ),
    v_K                     ( 0     ),
    v_W                     ( 0     ),
    v_Keep                  ( False ),
    v_UpA                   ( 0     ),
    v_UpB                   ( 0     ),
    v_BdA                   ( 0     ),
    v_BdB                   ( 0     ),
    v_h33                   ( False ),
    v_h35                   ( False ),
    v_h37                   ( False ),
    v_h13                   ( False ),
    v_h14                   ( False ),
    v_h41                   ( False ),
    v_h42                   ( False ),
    v_h43                   ( False ),
    v_h45                   ( False ),
    v_h47                   ( False ),
    v_h48                   ( False ),
    v_c33                   ( 0     ),
    v_c35                   ( 0     ),
    v_c37                   ( 0     ),
    v_c13                   ( 0     ),
    v_c14                   ( 0     ),
    v_c41                   ( 0     ),
    v_c42                   ( 0     ),
    v_c43                   ( 0     ),
    v_c45                   ( 0     ),
    v_c47                   ( 0     ),
    v_c48                   ( 0     ),
    v_NBars                 ( 0     ),
    v_Ymd                   ( 0     );

    { ---------- SECTION 1  SESSION.  Same construction as IND_S16S_P29
      SECTION 1 and IND_S16S_CONV6, deliberately -- a second implementation
      of the session counter is how two files start disagreeing. ---------- }

v_In_Day   = Time >  Sess_Day_Start   and Time <= Sess_Day_End;
v_In_Night = Time >  Sess_Night_Start or  Time <= Sess_Night_End;
v_In_Sess  = v_In_Day or v_In_Night;

v_Sess_First = False;
if CurrentBar > 1 then begin
    if v_In_Day   and ( v_In_Day[1]   = False ) then v_Sess_First = True;
    if v_In_Night and ( v_In_Night[1] = False ) then v_Sess_First = True;
end;

if v_Sess_First then
    v_BIS = 1
else if v_In_Sess then
    v_BIS = v_BIS + 1
else
    v_BIS = 0;

v_NBars = v_NBars + 1;

v_h33 = False;  v_h35 = False;  v_h37 = False;  v_h13 = False;
v_h14 = False;  v_h41 = False;  v_h42 = False;  v_h43 = False;
v_h45 = False;  v_h47 = False;  v_h48 = False;

    { ---------- SECTION 2  SESSION LOW.  Runs on EVERY bar, ahead of the
      guard, exactly as the scan does -- the low of a session that the
      guard skipped still has to be carried forward. ---------- }

if v_BIS[1] < v_BIS[2] then begin
    v_SessLo  = v_CurLo;
    v_SessSet = v_CurSet;
    v_CurLo   = Low[1];
    v_CurSet  = True;
end
else if ( v_CurSet = False ) or Low[1] < v_CurLo then begin
    v_CurLo  = Low[1];
    v_CurSet = True;
end;

    { ---------- SECTION 3  THE GUARD.  Skip when the classified bar is
      too early in its session, or when the bar AFTER it opens a new one --
      that second half is what forces the whole file one bar late. -------- }

v_Go = v_BIS[1] >= 2 and v_BIS >= v_BIS[1];

if v_Go then begin

    v_Rng = High[1] - Low[1];

    { ------ SECTION 4  PIVOT LEVEL.  Read the standing level, then arm
      or disarm it.  Each level is swept or broken at most once. ------ }

    if v_HiSet and v_ArmHi and High[1] > v_HiPv and Close[1] < v_HiPv then begin
        v_h33 = True;
        v_c33 = v_c33 + 1;
        v_ArmHi = False;
    end;

    if v_LoSet and v_ArmLo and Close[1] < v_LoPv then begin
        v_h35 = True;
        v_c35 = v_c35 + 1;
        if v_UpLast then begin
            v_h37 = True;
            v_c37 = v_c37 + 1;
        end;
        v_UpLast = False;
        v_ArmLo  = False;
    end;

    if v_HiSet and Close[1] > v_HiPv then v_UpLast = True;

    { ------ SECTION 5  BAR LEVEL. ------ }

    if v_BIS[1] >= 5
       and v_Rng > High[2] - Low[2]
       and v_Rng > High[3] - Low[3]
       and v_Rng > High[4] - Low[4] then begin
        v_h41 = True;
        v_c41 = v_c41 + 1;
    end;

    if v_BIS[1] >= 8
       and v_Rng > High[2] - Low[2]
       and v_Rng > High[3] - Low[3]
       and v_Rng > High[4] - Low[4]
       and v_Rng > High[5] - Low[5]
       and v_Rng > High[6] - Low[6]
       and v_Rng > High[7] - Low[7] then begin
        v_h42 = True;
        v_c42 = v_c42 + 1;
    end;

    if v_BIS[1] >= 3 and High[1] > High[2] and Close[1] < Low[2] then begin
        v_h43 = True;
        v_c43 = v_c43 + 1;
    end;

    if v_SessSet and v_BIS[1] >= 2 and Close[1] < v_SessLo then begin
        v_h45 = True;
        v_c45 = v_c45 + 1;
        v_SessSet = False;
    end;

    { horn: two spikes ONE BAR APART, both shadow-dominant, a dip between,
      highs closer together than the shorter shadow }
    if v_BIS[1] >= 4 then begin
        v_UpA = High[3] - MaxList( Open[3], Close[3] );
        v_BdA = AbsValue( Close[3] - Open[3] );
        v_UpB = High[1] - MaxList( Open[1], Close[1] );
        v_BdB = AbsValue( Close[1] - Open[1] );
        if v_UpA > v_BdA and v_UpB > v_BdB
           and High[3] > High[2] and High[1] > High[2]
           and AbsValue( High[3] - High[1] ) < MinList( v_UpA, v_UpB ) then begin
            v_h47 = True;
            v_c47 = v_c47 + 1;
        end;
    end;

    { pipe: the same test on two ADJACENT spikes }
    if v_BIS[1] >= 4 then begin
        v_UpA = High[2] - MaxList( Open[2], Close[2] );
        v_BdA = AbsValue( Close[2] - Open[2] );
        v_UpB = High[1] - MaxList( Open[1], Close[1] );
        v_BdB = AbsValue( Close[1] - Open[1] );
        if v_UpA > v_BdA and v_UpB > v_BdB
           and High[2] > High[3] and High[1] > High
           and AbsValue( High[2] - High[1] ) < MinList( v_UpA, v_UpB ) then begin
            v_h48 = True;
            v_c48 = v_c48 + 1;
        end;
    end;

    { ------ SECTION 6  BEAR FLAG AND PENNANT.  Pole, drift, resolution.
      The high is tested BEFORE the low: a bar that clears the pole high
      and closes under the pole low kills the flag without registering
      one, and that ordering is part of the definition. ------ }

    v_W = 0;
    if v_NPole > 0 then begin
    for v_K = 0 to v_NPole - 1 begin
        v_Keep = False;
        if High[1] <= v_PoH[v_K] then begin
            if Close[1] < v_PoL[v_K] then begin
                if v_PoN[v_K] >= 1 then begin
                    v_h13 = True;
                    v_c13 = v_c13 + 1;
                    if v_PoCv[v_K] > 0 then begin
                        v_h14 = True;
                        v_c14 = v_c14 + 1;
                    end;
                end;
            end
            else
                v_Keep = True;
        end;
        if v_Keep then begin
            if v_Rng >= v_PoLast[v_K] then v_PoCv[v_K] = 0;
            v_PoLast[v_K] = v_Rng;
            v_PoN[v_K]    = v_PoN[v_K] + 1;
            v_PoH[v_W]    = v_PoH[v_K];
            v_PoL[v_W]    = v_PoL[v_K];
            v_PoN[v_W]    = v_PoN[v_K];
            v_PoCv[v_W]   = v_PoCv[v_K];
            v_PoLast[v_W] = v_PoLast[v_K];
            v_W = v_W + 1;
        end;
    end;
    end;
    v_NPole = v_W;

    { a new pole is a WR4 bar that closed down }
    if v_BIS[1] >= 5 and Close[1] < Open[1]
       and v_Rng > High[2] - Low[2]
       and v_Rng > High[3] - Low[3]
       and v_Rng > High[4] - Low[4] then begin
        if v_NPole < 4 then begin
            v_PoH[v_NPole]    = High[1];
            v_PoL[v_NPole]    = Low[1];
            v_PoN[v_NPole]    = 0;
            v_PoCv[v_NPole]   = 1;
            v_PoLast[v_NPole] = v_Rng;
            v_NPole = v_NPole + 1;
        end
        else
            v_Ovf = v_Ovf + 1;
    end;

    { ------ SECTION 7  PUSH THE PIVOT for the bar just classified.  Last,
      because the scan pushes at the END of its iteration -- the level a
      break is measured against must be the one standing BEFORE this
      bar. ------ }

    if High[1] > High[2] and High[1] > High then begin
        v_HiPv  = High[1];
        v_HiSet = True;
        v_ArmHi = True;
    end;

    if Low[1] < Low[2] and Low[1] < Low then begin
        v_LoPv  = Low[1];
        v_LoSet = True;
        v_ArmLo = True;
    end;

end;

    { ---------- SECTION 8  THE RIBBON.  Every row plots on EVERY bar; the
      firing is carried by COLOUR.  A NoPlot-gapped plot made MC12
      interpolate a line across the whole chart on 2026-08-26. ---------- }

Plot1 (  1, "WR4"      );
Plot2 (  2, "WR7"      );
Plot3 (  3, "BearFlag" );
Plot4 (  4, "KeyRev"   );
Plot5 (  5, "Pennant"  );
Plot6 (  6, "HornTop"  );
Plot7 (  7, "PipeTop"  );
Plot8 (  8, "PrevSLow" );
Plot9 (  9, "BOS"      );
Plot10( 10, "Upthrust" );
Plot11( 11, "CHoCH"    );

if v_h41 and Enable_P41 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  1, Col_Bar   )
                             else SetPlotColor(  1, Col_Idle  );
if v_h42 and Enable_P42 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  2, Col_Bar   )
                             else SetPlotColor(  2, Col_Idle  );
if v_h13 and Enable_P13 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  3, Col_Flag  )
                             else SetPlotColor(  3, Col_Idle  );
if v_h43 and Enable_P43 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  4, Col_Bar   )
                             else SetPlotColor(  4, Col_Idle  );
if v_h14 and Enable_P14 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  5, Col_Flag  )
                             else SetPlotColor(  5, Col_Idle  );
if v_h47 and Enable_P47 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  6, Col_Bar   )
                             else SetPlotColor(  6, Col_Idle  );
if v_h48 and Enable_P48 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  7, Col_Bar   )
                             else SetPlotColor(  7, Col_Idle  );
if v_h45 and Enable_P45 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  8, Col_Bar   )
                             else SetPlotColor(  8, Col_Idle  );
if v_h35 and Enable_P35 <> 0 then SetPlotColor(  9, Col_Pivot )
                             else SetPlotColor(  9, Col_Idle  );
if v_h33 and Enable_P33 <> 0 then SetPlotColor( 10, Col_Pivot )
                             else SetPlotColor( 10, Col_Idle  );
if v_h37 and Enable_P37 <> 0 then SetPlotColor( 11, Col_Choch )
                             else SetPlotColor( 11, Col_Idle  );

    { ---------- SECTION 9  DIAGNOSTICS ---------- }

if Print_Events <> 0 and ( v_h37 or v_h45 ) then begin
    v_Ymd = Date + 19000000;
    Print( "ELEVEN EVENT ", v_Ymd:8:0, " ", Time:4:0,
           "  CHoCH=", v_c37:6:0, "  PrevSLow=", v_c45:6:0 );
end;

if CurrentBar = 1 then Print( "IND_S16S_ELEVEN build ", Build_ID:6:0 );

if LastBarOnChart then begin
    Print( "ELEVEN DIAG   bars=", v_NBars:8:0,
           "  pole_overflow=", v_Ovf:5:0,
           "  last=", ( Date + 19000000 ):8:0, " ", Time:4:0 );
    Print( "ELEVEN TALLY  P33=", v_c33:6:0, "  P35=", v_c35:6:0,
           "  P37=", v_c37:6:0, "  P13=", v_c13:6:0,
           "  P14=", v_c14:6:0, "  P41=", v_c41:6:0 );
    Print( "ELEVEN TALLY  P42=", v_c42:6:0, "  P43=", v_c43:6:0,
           "  P45=", v_c45:6:0, "  P47=", v_c47:6:0,
           "  P48=", v_c48:6:0 );
    Print( "ELEVEN REF     18003   24132   12675   12041    5883   82258" );
    Print( "ELEVEN REF     44455    8308    1463    5020    4973",
           "   (laptop csv, bars 421506, overflow 0)" );
end;
